### Toolchain Agent API Tests

This file exercises the interactive Toolchain Trail session API under
`/api/toolchain`. It covers the browser/game starting a session, the local
agent exchanging a one-time pairing code, the agent polling and submitting
evidence, and the game reading the session status.

Install the **REST Client** extension in VS Code and select the `local` or
`deployed` environment. Configure the same `baseUrl`, `adminUid`, and
`adminPassword` variables used by `cspathway.http` in the Git-ignored
`.vscode/settings.json`.

Run the requests in order. Pairing codes are single-use; start a new session
before pairing again. The agent token is a credential. Do not share or commit
response data. The sample evidence below deliberately fails, so it will not
mark a station complete. Replace it only with the actual output and exit codes
from the local agent when testing a successful check.

### 1. Authenticate the game/student

# @name loginToolchain
POST {{baseUrl}}/authenticate
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "uid": "{{adminUid}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 2. Start a station session and get a one-time pairing code

# @name startToolchainSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stationId": "terminal-town-gate"
}

### 3. Agent exchanges the one-time code for a scoped token

# @name pairToolchainAgent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/pair
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pairingCode": "{{startToolchainSession.response.body.$.pairingCode}}"
}

### 4. Agent polls for the station used to start the session

# @name pollToolchainAgent
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.sessionId}}/next
Authorization: Bearer {{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}

### 5. Game requests a check at the next station

# @name requestToolchainNextStation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.sessionId}}/check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stationId": "editor-isle-tower"
}

### 6. Agent polls for the newly requested station

# @name pollToolchainNextStation
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.sessionId}}/next
Authorization: Bearer {{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}

### 7. Agent submits evidence for the newly requested station

# This example intentionally reports failed checks. Replace the exit codes and
# output with actual `code --version` results from the local agent before testing a successful pass.
# @name submitToolchainResults
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.sessionId}}/results
Authorization: Bearer {{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.agentToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "os": "macos",
  "stationId": "editor-isle-tower",
  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "editor",
      "exitCode": 1,
      "output": "Example intentionally fails; replace with actual code --version output."
    }
  ]
}

### 8. Game reads the evaluated session/check status

# @name readToolchainSession
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/toolchain/sessions/{{pairToolchainAgent.response.body.$.sessionId}}
